--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party dependencies distributed with the Python package
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Python runtime is stdlib-only: the distribution declares no runtime dependency.
Development-only tooling is declared in pyproject.toml under
[project.optional-dependencies].dev (build, packaging, pip, setuptools, wheel) and is
used only to build and validate the distribution. The web frontend depends on the npm
packages pinned in web/package-lock.json (Astro, React, @astrojs/react, @astrojs/check,
TypeScript, @types/*, and the @fontsource variable/self-hosted font packages, which are
distributed under the SIL Open Font License and are not relicensed by Apache-2.0).

Third-party actions referenced by .github/workflows/ci.yml are the official
actions/checkout, actions/setup-python, and actions/setup-node actions, each used under
the GitHub Terms of Service for Actions.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Fixtures, datasets, and third-party-derived artifacts
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Fixtures, datasets, generated mockups, and visual references are NOT covered by the
Apache-2.0 code license. Every tracked such artifact has a row in the versioned
inventory at docs/licensing/fixture-inventory.v1.json, with a human-readable summary at
docs/licensing/README.md. Each row records provenance, license or terms evidence,
required attribution, modifications, personal-data class, and redistribution status.

Rows whose rights evidence is unresolved are held at redistribution status
`pending-review` or `blocked` and must not be included in a release artifact or a
public projection until the recorded owner and legal review (DP-304, DP-305, DP-306,
DP-307) are complete. The Apache License 2.0 is not a grant for media, transcripts,
evidence bodies, datasets, or platform content.

At the current review date, real public-source material collected from Instagram,
TikTok, and YouTube (Raffaele Giuliani and Beppe Grillo content) is `blocked` for
redistribution: public availability is not a permission, and those platforms' terms
reserve rights. Visual references under docs/ux/reference/p6.2/ have unknown origin and
are `pending-review`.
